Package: sonicray
Type: Package
Title: Metal GPU Path Tracing and Compositing of Light-Layer Films on Apple Silicon
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Matthew", "Ross", email = "matthew.r.v.ross@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
  )
Description: GPU (Metal) path tracing of per-light 'light layers' and a GPU compositor that turns them into
    films, for 3D sensor-network and environmental-data visualisation on Apple Silicon. Light is linear, so a frame is a
    weighted sum of layers: render each light once on the GPU, then re-time and re-colour freely. Inspired by, and an
    attempt to follow, the work of Tyler Morgan-Wall (rayshader, rayrender); not affiliated with him and containing none of
    his code. Written with AI assistance (Anthropic Claude Sonnet 5.5, via Claude Code); see AI_ATTRIBUTION.md.
License: GPL-3
URL: https://github.com/matthewross07/sonic_ray
BugReports: https://github.com/matthewross07/sonic_ray/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
OS_type: unix
SystemRequirements: GNU make, macOS >= 14 on Apple Silicon (Metal 3), Xcode Command Line Tools, ffmpeg
Depends:
    R (>= 4.3.0)
Imports:
    Rcpp (>= 1.0.12),
    jsonlite,
    png,
    stats,
    utils
LinkingTo:
    Rcpp
Suggests:
    rayrender